
 This is the application most C++ programmers want to see:
 How to handle heterogenous lists with virtual functions.
 The example has a linked list of Shapes, that can be either Squares
 or Rectangles. The entry pointer to the list is encapsulated under
 Root. Root and Shapes form a COLLECTION.

 In one command, util.save(), the entire data organization is saved to
 disk, then util.open() retrieves the data back to memory.

 In order to run the program, type:   test < inp > out
 The results will be deposited into file 'out'.
